<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ya'qub ibn al-Layth al-Saffar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">840–879</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ya'qub ibn al-Layth al-Saffar was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saffarid-dynasty">Saffarid dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. A coppersmith turned leader of local volunteer fighters, he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaranj">Zaranj</a> in 861 and conquered much of Iran and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, overthrowing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirids</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nishapur">Nishapur</a> in 873. His march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> was defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a> in 876, and he died in 879.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yaqub-ibn-al-layth-al-saffar.jpg" alt="Ya'qub ibn al-Layth al-Saffar" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sotheby's · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_illustrated_and_illuminated_folio_from_a_manuscript_of_Husayn_Va%E2%80%99iz_al-Kashifi%E2%80%99s_Akhlaq-i_Muhsini;_Ya%27qub_ibn_Layth_standing_on_the_roof_in_full_armour,_Persia,_Shiraz,_Safavid,_16th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
